===Etymology 1===
From {{term|used||lang=en}}, past participle of {{term|use#Verb|use|lang=en|to perform habitually}} + {{term|to#Preposition|to}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|head=[[used]] [[to#Preposition|to]]}}

# {{idiomatic|with noun phrase}} [[accustomed]] to, tolerant or accepting of.
#: ''I am '''used to''' cleaning up other people’s mess.''
#: ''I became '''used to''' his ways.''
#* '''1922''', {{w|Margery Williams}}, ''{{w|The Velveteen Rabbit}}''
#*: He was shivering a little, for he had always been '''used to''' sleeping in a proper bed, and by this time his coat had worn so thin and threadbare from hugging that it was no longer any protection to him.

